<h2>Other communities in Tippah County</h2>

<p>Several smaller unincorporated communities appear on Tippah County maps and in local usage without having their own municipal government or census count. They include <strong>Cotton Plant</strong>, <strong>Brownfield</strong>, <strong>Dry Creek</strong>, <strong>Lake Mohawk</strong> and <strong>Camp Hill</strong>. Residents of these communities are served by Tippah County offices in Ripley and by either the North Tippah or South Tippah school district, depending on location.</p>

<h2>How the county is organized</h2>

<p>Tippah County's two school districts split the county roughly north and south. The <strong>North Tippah School District</strong> serves Walnut, Falkner, Chalybeate and Tiplersville from a central office at 20821 Highway 15 in Falkner. The <strong>South Tippah School District</strong> serves Ripley, Blue Mountain, Dumas and Pine Grove from 402 Greenlee Street in Ripley.</p>

<p>Law enforcement outside the Ripley city limits is handled by the Tippah County Sheriff's Department at 205 West Spring Street in Ripley, 662-837-9336. In an emergency, call 911.</p>

